§§ `15.1.4: overloading between 20% and 50%`

GIVEN `the load` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A claim`
`the standard collision of a goods vehicle permitted 1000, carrying` `the load` MEANS
    `a claim: vehicle` (`a goods vehicle permitted to carry` 1000) `, policy` `the standard policy` `, claimant` `the insured named on the certificate`
        `, event` `the event` `, driving` `the standard driving` `, conduct` `prompt and proper conduct` `, shortfall` `no premium shortfall` `, costs` `no costs`
        `, hire` NOTHING `, wreck` `no wreck kept` `, other insurance` EMPTY
    WHERE
        `the event` MEANS
            `an event on` (YMD 2026 6 15) `: peril` `a collision` `, sudden` TRUE `, at` `in Vietnam` `, war` FALSE `, deliberate` EMPTY
                `, hired out` FALSE `, inspection` `a valid inspection certificate` `, load` (`carrying` `the load` `, with persons` 2 `, and children under 7` 0) `, parts` `the standard parts`
                `, paint` NOTHING `, police suspension` FALSE `, earlier part thefts` 0

-- 30% over: 30% off (16.5m x 0.7 - 0.5m). 20% over: nothing. 49.9% over: 49.9% off.
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the standard collision of a goods vehicle permitted 1000, carrying` 1300) EQUALS 11_050_000
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the standard collision of a goods vehicle permitted 1000, carrying` 1200) EQUALS 16_000_000
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the standard collision of a goods vehicle permitted 1000, carrying` 1499) EQUALS 7_766_500
#ASSERT `the amount payable on` (`the standard collision of a goods vehicle permitted 1000, carrying` 1500) EQUALS 0

